  "summary": "I reviewed Harold Vance's medications against RBC-PHARM-07. Only gabapentin needed a change. Apixaban and metformin stay as they are.\n\n**Values I used**\n- **Creatinine:** 1.21 mg/dL from 10/20. The 1.88 from 10/21 is marked entered-in-error because the specimen was mislabelled and belongs to another patient.\n- **Weight:** 64.9 kg (143 lb), measured 10/20. The 132 lb entry from 10/22 is his own estimate by phone, not a measured weight, so I left it out.\n- **Age:** 82.\n\n**The pharmacy screen used the wrong creatinine.** The pharmacist's 10/21 note was based on the 1.88 result. That gave kidney numbers of 35 (eGFR) and 28 (creatinine clearance), and suggestions of metformin 500 mg twice daily and gabapentin 300 mg once daily. With the valid 1.21, neither suggestion holds.\n\n**Results by drug**\n- **Apixaban 2.5 mg twice daily: no change.** The policy's apixaban section covers atrial fibrillation only. He has no AF diagnosis; he takes it as long-term prevention after 6 months of treatment for a PE. Hematology wrote that 2.5 mg twice daily should continue indefinitely and is not a kidney-adjusted dose. Applying the AF criteria would have been wrong: only his age meets them, which would point to 5 mg twice daily.\n- **Metformin 1000 mg twice daily: no change.** eGFR is 59.8, and the policy only reduces the dose below 45.\n- **Gabapentin: reduced from 600 mg three times daily (1800 mg/day) to 600 mg twice daily (1200 mg/day).** Creatinine clearance is 43.2 mL/min, so the policy allows 400–1400 mg/day given twice daily. I modified the existing order on the same 600 mg tablet; the new order is mr-t0001 and the old one is stopped and linked.\n\nHis other active medications aren't covered by the policy, so I didn't change them.\n\n**Note:** I signed a progress note (doc-t0002) with the values, the result of each rule, the change and the cited results. It suggests asking how his nerve pain is controlled on the lower gabapentin dose, and getting a repeat creatinine and a measured weight at his next visit.\n\nI found no inbox item for Mr. Vance to close. Your results inbox has two critical-high potassium results from 10/22 for other patients (pt-0008 at 6.4 and pt-0010 at 6.2) that need attention.",
  "resumed": false,
